  "description": "Uniswap's Permit2 (spec section 15.9, experimental): its AllowanceTransfer messages (PermitSingle, PermitBatch), which set allowances, and its SignatureTransfer messages (PermitTransferFrom, PermitBatchTransferFrom), which authorize one transfer. Witness messages (PermitWitnessTransferFrom) are left out: each protocol adds its own witness type, in a profile of its own (O9; x402's is x402-exact-permit2). Bound to the deployments ERC-7730's own Permit2 example lists (chains 1 and 42161) and to Base and Base Sepolia (8453 and 84532), whose Permit2 code and domain were read on chain on 2026-10-30, so a look-alike contract named \"Permit2\" gets none of these words. Amounts are in the token the message names: a consumer supplies that token's decimals() and symbol(), and shows its address beside the symbol.",
